NAME: trawl
LAST DEPLOYED: Mon Sep 28 11:38:52 2026
NAMESPACE: trawl-auto
STATUS: deployed
REVISION: 1
DESCRIPTION: Install complete
NOTES:
Trawl has been installed.

Create roles and API keys against the Fleet database:
  https://trawl.sh/operate/access/#create-roles-and-keys
Use a personal API key to sign in to the browser and a service key for each collector.
The init-auth container initializes the database schema; it does not create API keys.

The daemon generates a self-signed certificate. For trusted remote API access, choose tls.mode=secret or certManager:
  https://trawl.sh/operate/deployment/#configure-the-daemon-api-certificate

Browser-ingress TLS is configured separately through ingress.tls.

Check the HTTPS API through a local port-forward:

  kubectl port-forward --namespace trawl-auto svc/trawl 5514:5514

Keep the port-forward running. In another terminal on this machine:

  curl --fail-with-body --insecure https://localhost:5514/api/v1/health

Expect status "ok" and every entry in "checks" to be "ok". HTTP 200 alone can
report degraded dependencies. --insecure is only for this local check.

Configured browser origins:
  http://localhost:8090

For the configured local browser origin, keep this port-forward running:

  kubectl port-forward --namespace trawl-auto svc/trawl 8090:8090

Open http://localhost:8090 and sign in with your personal API key.

